.TH TEST 1
.SH NAME
test \- evaluate a condition, for use by shell scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B test
.I expression
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Test
evaluates
.I expression
and exits with status false if the value is
.BR "" (empty)
or
.BR 0 ,
true otherwise \(em the venerable shell-scripting
.B test
command, unary and binary operators included:
.TP
.BI -f " file"
.I File
exists and is a plain file.
.TP
.BI -d " file"
.I File
exists and is a directory.
.TP
.BI -e " file"
.I File
exists.
.TP
.BI -r " file" ", " -w " file" ", " -x " file"
.I File
exists and is readable, writable, or executable respectively.
.TP
.BI -s " file"
.I File
exists and has non-zero length.
.TP
.BI -z " string" ", " -n " string"
.I String
has zero length, or non-zero length.
.TP
.IR n1 " -eq " n2 ", " -ne ", " -gt ", " -lt ", " -ge ", " -le " n2"
Integer comparison.
.TP
.IR file1 " -nt " file2 ", " -ot " file2"
.I File1
is newer, or older, than
.IR file2 .
.TP
.IR file " -older " time
.I File\^'s
modification time is older than
.IR time .
.PP
Expressions combine with
.B -a
(and),
.B -o
(or), and parentheses; a leading
.B !
negates.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/test.b
